# Each record replaces the old article's unverified anecdotes and stale facts.
# Keys match the ordered source archive; original URL slugs are preserved.
ARTICLES={
0:('Add a Download Button to Your Shopify Thank-You Page','Delivery','Give customers access while their purchase is still in front of them. A post-purchase download button complements email delivery and gives buyers another way to retrieve the product.',[
('Start with the right checkout surface','The thank-you page and order-status page are related but distinct. Use the app’s supported Shopify extension or integration for the current checkout experience. Do not paste a public file URL into a generic text block: that can bypass the purchase-based access you intended.'),
('Check the paid-order journey','Create a test order for a product with a real file attached. Confirm that the correct download appears after payment, then reopen the order-status link. A mixed physical and digital cart should clearly identify which item is downloadable and which will ship.'),
('Keep an email recovery route','Some customers close checkout before downloading or complete the order on another device. Keep a branded delivery email and a clear support route. Test the message in more than one inbox and avoid relying on a single browser tab.'),
('Test the edge cases','Verify a bundle, a variant and a custom or scheduled product if you sell them. Scheduled content should not become available early. A custom order should explain when the finished file will arrive rather than displaying a broken or misleading instant-download promise.')]),
1:('Best Free Digital Download Apps for Shopify: Compare the Limits','Compare','A free plan is useful when its limits match your launch. Compare products, orders, storage and required features separately; a free installation is not always a free ongoing service.',[
('Choose the limit you will hit first','A 200 MB ebook catalogue and a 3 GB video product have very different needs. Write down catalogue storage, expected orders and the transfer volume of a promotion before installing. Leave room for updated files and repeat downloads.'),
('What BIG’s free plan includes','BIG’s current listing shows 250 MB storage, 50 orders, unlimited products and unlimited licence keys. PDF stamping belongs to paid plans. Do not use older articles that quote 500 MB, three products or 15 orders as today’s BIG limits.'),
('When another free option fits','Shopify Digital Products is free and supports files and links. Fileflare advertises a free 1 GB allowance with unlimited bandwidth. LDT’s free plan lists 500 MB and 30 orders per month. Each has different workflows; free capacity alone is not a complete feature comparison.'),
('Set an upgrade trigger before launch','Decide what should cause an upgrade: a storage threshold, a planned promotion, PDF protection or an integration. For a paid-plan comparison with current sources, use our app guide rather than assuming a free tier will handle every future launch.')]),
2:('Low-Cost Shopify Apps for Digital Products: A Practical Budget Guide','Compare','The cheapest workable setup is the one that delivers your products without hidden operational work. Compare app fees with capacity, order charges and the features you actually need.',[
('Start from your delivery requirements','List files, licence keys, custom orders and scheduled releases. Add PDF stamping only if you sell PDFs, and API access only if you have a workflow that uses it. Buying an advanced tier for a feature you never use does not improve delivery.'),
('Compare paid entry tiers fairly','BIG Starter is $9.99 with 15 GB storage and 50 GB monthly transfer. Filemonk Lite is $10 with 10 GB storage. LDT Starter is $8.99 with 15 GB and advertised unlimited bandwidth. These are different offers, not a universal price ranking.'),
('Look past the monthly headline','EDP’s paid tiers include 100 monthly digital orders and charge $0.15 for additional orders. SendOwl also considers annual sales and order volume. Storage, transfer and extra-order charges can change which app is economical for your store.'),
('Budget for the whole store','The digital-delivery app is one line in your costs. Keep Shopify subscription, payment fees, advertising, refunds and content production separate. Our revenue calculator uses editable assumptions so an example fee is never mistaken for your actual payment rate.')]),
3:('Sell Books on Shopify or a Marketplace? A Decision Guide','Ebooks & PDFs','Choose your book-sales channel based on discovery, customer experience and the work you are willing to own. A direct storefront and a marketplace can play different roles in a publishing business.',[
('Understand where readers will come from','A Shopify store gives you control over its product pages and purchase journey, but it does not bring a ready-made audience. Plan the source of demand: an existing newsletter, search traffic, partnerships or paid acquisition. Marketplace discovery also requires work and is not a guaranteed sale.'),
('Compare proceeds with like-for-like costs','Use the actual royalty or fee terms for your format, territory and price. On a direct store, subtract payment processing, Shopify, your delivery app and acquisition costs. Do not describe the remaining revenue as pure profit while leaving editing and marketing out.'),
('Check exclusivity before selling direct','Amazon’s KDP Select programme requires digital exclusivity during its enrolment period. That is different from simply publishing through KDP. Check your title’s enrolment status before offering the same ebook on your own store.'),
('Build a reader-friendly package','Offer a clearly described PDF or EPUB, plus a short guide to opening it on common devices. Show a sample chapter and list the included formats before purchase. If you add PDF stamping, test that it does not cover diagrams or make the text difficult to read.')]),
4:('Selling Textbooks Online: Resale, Original Guides and Real Costs','Ebooks & PDFs','Selling a used physical textbook and selling a digital study guide are different businesses. Start by identifying what you own, what you can distribute and how much work each channel requires.',[
('For physical resale, compare net proceeds','Match the exact ISBN, edition and condition when collecting buyback quotes or researching marketplace sales. Subtract fees, packaging, shipping and the time needed to handle messages. An advertised listing price is not proof that a book sells at that price.'),
('For digital sales, start with your own material','An original revision guide, practice worksheet or set of notes can be a digital product. Owning a printed textbook does not by itself grant permission to scan and sell copies. Verify your rights and any institutional restrictions before publishing material.'),
('Describe the educational scope','List the subject, level, edition alignment and what is excluded. A practice pack should distinguish original exercises from official exam content. Provide sample pages so a buyer can assess whether the material fits their course.'),
('Package useful study bundles','A guide, answer sheet and printable revision planner can make a coherent bundle when they solve the same problem. Keep answers in a separate file, provide an accessible version where possible and state how corrections or updated editions will be handled.')]),
5:('Moving from SendOwl to Shopify: An Alternatives and Migration Guide','Compare','A migration should solve a concrete problem: a changing bill, a missing workflow or the desire to run fulfilment inside Shopify. Start by auditing the parts of SendOwl you actually use.',[
('Separate checkout from fulfilment','SendOwl can provide off-platform checkout and marketing tools as well as delivery. A Shopify-focused delivery app does not automatically replace payment links, subscriptions or an affiliate programme. Identify those dependencies before cancelling.'),
('Model your actual usage','SendOwl’s current pricing uses annual sales and orders as well as monthly transfer. BIG paid plans use storage and bandwidth without an order-count cap. Use normal and peak months, and include external services you would need to replace.'),
('Protect existing customer access','Export the data your current plan supports and back up original files. Map products, variants and licence inventories. Do not assume old SendOwl links will keep working after cancellation; ask about their lifecycle and verify previous-order access in the new setup.'),
('Pick the alternative for the reason you are leaving','BIG is an option for custom, scheduled and standard Shopify delivery. Fileflare is worth comparing for unlimited bandwidth; Sky Pilot for streaming and integrations. See the dedicated alternatives page for sourced pricing and candid limitations.')]),
6:('How to Choose a Shopify Digital Download App in 2026','Compare','There is no useful universal winner for a tiny PDF store, a software vendor and a video publisher. A good shortlist starts with the customer journey and the workload behind it.',[
('Compare the same job','File delivery, licence inventory, streaming and a full course platform are different jobs. Write a short acceptance checklist for your store. A long feature list is only helpful if you know which features must work together.'),
('Make capacity concrete','Estimate the size of the catalogue and monthly transfer separately. A 100 MB purchase downloaded 1,000 times transfers about 100 GB before retries. Unlimited products, orders and download count do not necessarily include unlimited bandwidth.'),
('Use documentation, then a test purchase','Public listings establish what a provider claims. A trial establishes whether the workflow fits you. Test the email, checkout access, mobile download and one exception such as a wrong email address or a scheduled release.'),
('Understand who wrote the recommendation','This guide is published by BIG. We explain our strengths and link to the original sources, but it is not an independent benchmark. Our permanent comparison pages also state where another app offers lower cost or stronger capacity.')]),
7:('BIG or Fileflare? Choose by Catalogue Size and Transfer Volume','Compare','Fileflare’s unlimited bandwidth is a real advantage for heavy downloads. BIG can be attractive at a lower paid entry price when you need a modest protected catalogue and its Shopify delivery workflow.',[
('A small protected catalogue','BIG Starter includes PDF stamping, 15 GB storage and 50 GB monthly bandwidth for $9.99. Fileflare Basic includes stamping and 50 GB storage at $19 with unlimited bandwidth. Decide whether the extra transfer and storage justify the difference for your store.'),
('A large library or video business','Fileflare Premium lists 1 TB and unlimited bandwidth at $39. BIG Growth is $49.99 for 1 TB storage and 1 TB transfer. BIG is not the capacity-price winner in that comparison; consider workflow and support fit rather than ignoring the numbers.'),
('Developer requirements matter','Fileflare lists REST API access on Basic. BIG’s API and outgoing webhooks are on Growth and Enterprise. Check the endpoints and events you need with each provider before assuming both integrations are interchangeable.'),
('Avoid comparing the wrong plan names','Some older articles call Fileflare’s $39 plan Growth. The current listing calls it Premium. Use the live listing and our dated comparison table when calculating costs, and recheck before subscribing.')]),
8:('When to Move Beyond Shopify’s Free Digital Products App','Compare','Move when a specific requirement is unmet, not simply because your store has started making sales. Shopify’s free app remains a reasonable option for straightforward file and link delivery.',[
('Write down the missing workflow','A need for buyer-specific PDF stamping, unique licence inventory, custom fulfilment or a scheduled launch is more useful than a vague desire for a better app. Test whether your current setup can meet that requirement first.'),
('Use the current Shopify product','The official app is now listed as Shopify Digital Products. Its description includes files, links, variants and customer-account access. Older comparisons that claim all of those are absent should not decide your migration.'),
('Make the case for BIG precisely','BIG offers standard, custom and scheduled products, paid-plan PDF stamping and order/key exports. Those features may justify moving. Its paid plans still have storage and transfer limits, so model your volume before upgrading.'),
('Switch without duplicate messages','Run controlled test orders before changing live fulfilment. Check how historical orders are handled, then disable duplicate delivery messages deliberately. Do not leave two apps sending conflicting instructions to every buyer.')]),
9:('20 Digital Product Ideas to Validate Before You Build','Ideas & growth','An idea is a starting hypothesis, not proof of demand. Choose a specific buyer and a repeatable task, then test a small useful product before building a large catalogue.',[
('Twenty starting points','1. Budget worksheet; 2. Meal planner; 3. Lesson pack; 4. Original revision guide; 5. Onboarding checklist; 6. Notion project system; 7. Canva social kit; 8. Lightroom preset pack; 9. Original stock photography; 10. Icon set; 11. Audio sample library; 12. Sound effects; 13. Ebook; 14. Video workshop; 15. Sewing pattern; 16. 3D model; 17. Software utility; 18. Printable game; 19. Custom digital portrait; 20. Industry-specific spreadsheet.'),
('Choose a buyer before a format','A spreadsheet for freelance cash flow is easier to describe than a spreadsheet for everyone. Identify the moment when a buyer needs help, the information they already have and what a successful result looks like.'),
('Test willingness to pay honestly','Show a sample, a clear scope and a real price to relevant people. If taking preorders, state when delivery happens and what is included. Interest, likes and downloads of a free sample are different signals from a paid purchase.'),
('Design the first support experience','Include opening instructions, compatibility requirements and a contact route. A small product with a clear outcome is easier to improve than a huge bundle whose buyers cannot find the starting point. Track questions and update the product accordingly.')]),
10:('What GTA VI’s Extended Look Can Teach Digital Product Creators','Ideas & growth','A high-profile game reveal can suggest content ideas, but it does not prove that a specific digital product will sell. Treat the attention around GTA VI as a research prompt, not a revenue forecast.',[
('Separate attention from purchase intent','Rockstar published an Extended Look for GTA VI in August 2026. That confirms an event, not demand for an unrelated store’s templates or guides. Look for an audience task you can solve without making unsupported claims about sales.'),
('Build an original adjacent product','A generic stream-planning workbook, gaming-session journal or creator production checklist can be useful beyond one release. Create your own artwork and copy. Do not package game footage, logos, maps, music or characters as assets to resell without permission.'),
('Validate one audience and one use','A streamer planning a launch-week schedule has different needs from a casual player tracking games. Interview relevant users, show a small sample and make the offer understandable without leaning entirely on the game’s name.'),
('Plan for a short-lived search spike','A release-linked page may lose relevance after launch. Give the product an evergreen purpose, update time-sensitive wording and avoid describing an untested idea as proven. A smaller useful audience can be more valuable than broad curiosity.')]),
11:('Digital Products Around a Game Launch: A Shopify Planning Guide','Ideas & growth','A major game launch can be a deadline for an original creator product. The useful work is selecting a buyer, preparing delivery and leaving room for a release schedule to change.',[
('Use the official release source','As reviewed on 22 September 2026, Rockstar’s official GTA VI materials give 19 November 2026 as the release date. Recheck the official announcement before committing to a dated campaign. Do not treat a publisher’s schedule as a guarantee for your own business.'),
('Choose products with an independent use','Consider an original streaming planner, community event checklist or content-production template. The product should remain useful even if a game date changes. Avoid implying an official partnership or including protected game assets without permission.'),
('Build backwards from delivery','Allow time for a sample, buyer feedback, file preparation, a test purchase and support instructions. If using a scheduled digital product, confirm the timezone and make the unlock time visible to the customer before purchase.'),
('Keep preorders specific','State exactly what buyers receive, what is still being created and when you intend to deliver. Avoid promises of access to the game itself unless you are authorised to sell that access. A preparation template is not a game code.')]),
12:('Electronic Software Distribution on Shopify: Files, Keys and Updates','Software & licences','Electronic software distribution is more than sending an installer. A workable setup connects the correct version, the buyer’s licence and clear installation instructions.',[
('Keep delivery and activation separate','BIG can deliver software files and licence keys. Your application or licensing service must decide whether a key activates the product, how many devices it permits and how revocation works. A delivered string is not an activation system.'),
('Package for the supported environment','Name operating systems and versions explicitly. Keep Windows, macOS or other installers mapped to the right product variant. Include a version number, release notes and the support policy in the download package.'),
('Design an update policy before selling','Tell buyers whether the price covers a major version, a period of updates or future releases. Keep previous installers where your policy requires them. Test whether a product-file update affects past buyers before using it for a rollout.'),
('Track exceptions','Plan how to handle an empty key pool, a failed activation, a refund and a device replacement. Keep order and key exports secure. Only collect information required for the licensing and support workflow.')]),
13:('Bundle and Upsell Digital Products on Shopify Without Confusing Buyers','Ideas & growth','A useful bundle solves a larger version of the same problem. Start with a coherent outcome, then make the included files and licence terms easy to understand.',[
('Build around a job, not a file count','An ebook, worksheet and implementation checklist can work together. A hundred unrelated files can create more searching and support. Name the outcome of the bundle and show buyers where to begin.'),
('Make the price comparison honest','If you show a saving, compare against real individual prices and the same licence scope. A bundle discount based on invented reference prices undermines trust. Explain whether updates and future additions are included.'),
('Map every component to delivery','Use a delivery setup that connects the correct files to the bundle product or variant. Test a purchase after adding or replacing a component. Include a contents document so a buyer can tell whether the download is complete.'),
('Keep upsells optional and relevant','Suggest the next useful product after the buyer understands the current offer. Check that your chosen Shopify upsell tool and delivery app handle the resulting order correctly. Do not assume a delivery app also provides the upsell placement itself.')]),
14:('Create a Digital Product from Scratch: From Problem to First Sale','Ideas & growth','Start with a problem you understand well enough to solve. A small complete product is easier to validate, deliver and improve than a broad promise with months of production behind it.',[
('Define the outcome','Write one sentence describing who the product is for and what they can do after using it. Exclude needs outside that scope. This sentence should guide the contents, product page and support boundaries.'),
('Create the smallest useful version','For a guide, draft the actionable chapter before designing the cover. For a template, test the workflow with realistic sample data. For a course, record one complete lesson and its exercise before producing the full library.'),
('Get feedback from the intended buyer','Ask testers to use the product without you narrating every step. Record where they hesitate, what they expected and what they could not open. Fix the biggest usability gap before adding more material.'),
('Launch a clear offer','Show a sample, exact contents, compatibility, licence terms and delivery timing. Choose standard, custom or scheduled fulfilment to match reality. Treat early support questions as evidence for the next revision, not as a reason to promise everything.')]),
15:('Deliver Software Licence Keys Automatically on Shopify','Software & licences','A good licence-key workflow sends each buyer the correct key, keeps the inventory consistent and makes activation support manageable. Begin with your licensing model, then connect delivery.',[
('Decide what a key means','Specify product, edition, activation count and duration in your own licensing system. BIG delivers the key; it does not make an arbitrary code valid inside your software. Avoid mixing trial and paid keys in one inventory.'),
('Prepare and map the inventory','Clean duplicates and map keys to the correct Shopify product or variant. Keep a secure backup. Test which key is assigned to a controlled order and verify it activates the intended edition.'),
('Handle depleted stock and retries','Know what the customer sees when no usable key remains. Do not let a marketing promise of instant access outrun your inventory process. Test duplicate or retried order events so support can distinguish delivery from activation issues.'),
('Plan exports and revocation','Keep order-to-key records for support. A refund does not necessarily revoke a key in an external activation system automatically. Confirm and implement the process your licensing service needs; use BIG’s API and webhooks only on a plan that includes them.')]),
16:('Digital Products After the 2026 World Cup: What to Reuse Next','Ideas & growth','The 2026 tournament is over. A useful seasonal catalogue now needs a post-event plan: remove outdated promises, learn from actual buyer behaviour and adapt original designs for future events.',[
('Audit dated products','Check dates, fixtures and headlines before running another promotion. Archive products that only make sense during the completed tournament, or describe them honestly as commemorative material. Do not advertise an upcoming match that has already happened.'),
('Reuse the structure, not protected branding','An original match journal, generic scorecard or watch-party checklist can become an evergreen sports product. Review rights before using competition marks, team badges, player images or broadcast assets.'),
('Look at your own results','Review product-page visits, purchases, support questions and refund reasons. A popular social post does not tell you whether the product sold profitably. Keep the format that helped buyers and revise the parts they found confusing.'),
('Build a future-event workflow','Separate the reusable layout from dates and event data. Keep a source checklist for fixtures, a date for final review and a test print. This makes the next seasonal update more deliberate than changing only the year in a headline.')]),
17:('Protect Digital Products on Shopify: Five Practical Layers','Delivery','You can reduce unauthorised sharing, but no downloadable file is impossible to copy. Combine sensible access controls with a purchase experience that legitimate customers can use easily.',[
('Layers 1 and 2: clear rights and controlled access','State the licence scope before checkout and include it in the download package. Deliver through the app’s purchase-based access route rather than a public cloud link that anyone can forward. Avoid collecting unnecessary personal data for protection.'),
('Layer 3: reasonable download limits','Set enough attempts for a failed connection and a second device. Too strict a limit creates support work without preventing someone from copying an already-downloaded file. Test how a legitimate buyer requests renewed access.'),
('Layer 4: PDF stamping','A buyer-specific watermark can discourage casual redistribution. BIG’s documented stamping workflow uses an unprotected PDF. Test small pages, dark backgrounds and diagrams so the stamp does not damage the product.'),
('Layer 5: an incident response','Keep evidence of your original work and the unauthorised distribution you find. Follow the relevant platform’s reporting process and review the facts before making a claim. Improve controls where useful without describing any app as an absolute piracy guarantee.')]),
18:('Sell Digital Art on Shopify: Files, Prints and Licence Options','Design & templates','Selling an artwork as a downloadable file is different from granting commercial use or shipping a physical print. A clear product page distinguishes these offers before the customer buys.',[
('Define the deliverable','List formats, pixel dimensions, aspect ratios and the intended printing sizes. If a physical print is not included, state that near the purchase button. Show preview images that accurately represent the file, not only a decorative room mockup.'),
('Keep licences understandable','Explain personal versus commercial use in your own terms and identify any restrictions. Check rights for fonts, textures, stock assets and commissioned material used in the artwork. Selling a file does not automatically transfer copyright.'),
('Package versions for real use','Offer a logical folder structure and simple instructions for choosing the right aspect ratio. Include a small preview or readme. Test that ZIP files open on common devices and that the final image matches the advertised resolution.'),
('Offer custom work with custom delivery','A personalised portrait or bespoke design should use a made-to-order workflow. State the brief, revision allowance and expected delivery timing. Keep finished deliverables associated with the correct customer order.')]),
19:('Sell Canva Templates on Shopify: Links, Licensing and Delivery','Design & templates','A Canva template product usually delivers access to an editable design, not ownership of the original working file. The experience should help buyers make their own copy without changing your master.',[
('Prepare the template and access link','Start from your original design and use Canva’s appropriate template-sharing workflow. Test the link from a separate account. Do not send an edit link that lets customers alter the master design for everyone.'),
('Check the content licence','Canva has specific rules for selling templates and using Pro content. Its guidance permits Pro content in templates made for use on Canva through template links, subject to the licence. Check the current terms and disclose any paid features the buyer may need.'),
('Deliver a useful start document','A short PDF can contain the template link, duplication instructions, font notes and support contact. Put compatibility and required Canva access on the product page as well. A watermark on the PDF does not make the linked template impossible to share.'),
('Maintain the customer copy','Test every link after a significant template update. Explain whether customers receive updates automatically or need a new copy. Keep versions organised so a support request can be matched to what the buyer received.')]),
20:('Sell Digital Downloads on Shopify: A Complete Launch Checklist','Delivery','Shopify handles the storefront and checkout; a digital-delivery setup connects the purchase to the files or keys. Build the product and test the full customer journey before opening sales.',[
('Create a precise product listing','Describe the outcome, exact contents, format, compatibility and licence scope. Make clear that the item is digital and configure shipping appropriately for the product. Show a sample that reflects the actual download.'),
('Connect the product to the deliverable','Install BIG, upload the files or prepare access links and licence keys, then map them to the correct product and variant. Choose standard, custom or scheduled delivery according to when the customer should receive access.'),
('Make access visible','Check both the delivery email and the Shopify post-purchase experience. Use branded wording that states how to open the files and where to get help. A mobile test often reveals instructions that looked obvious on a desktop.'),
('Plan the first busy month','Estimate storage and monthly bandwidth, including repeat downloads. Choose a plan around the workload and required features. Monitor real usage after launch and before promoting a large video or multi-file bundle.')]),
21:('Sell Ebooks and PDFs on Shopify Alongside Your Publishing Strategy','Ebooks & PDFs','Direct ebook sales give you a storefront you can shape around your readers. They also make you responsible for discovery, delivery, support and the practical cost of acquiring a customer.',[
('Check your publishing commitments','If the ebook is enrolled in KDP Select, Amazon requires digital exclusivity during the enrolment period. Do not offer the same digital book on Shopify until your agreement allows it. Ordinary KDP publishing and KDP Select are not the same programme.'),
('Choose reader-friendly formats','PDF suits a fixed layout; EPUB is useful when readers need text to reflow. State the formats included and provide opening instructions. If you offer both, test both instead of assuming the export preserved every table or image.'),
('Sell a clear edition','Show a sample chapter, table of contents and edition date. Explain whether future corrections or major updates are included. A premium bundle should add useful material such as exercises or audio, not only increase the file count.'),
('Protect without obstructing reading','Use PDF stamping where appropriate and avoid covering text or diagrams. Give buyers enough download attempts for their devices. Protection can discourage sharing, but a purchase should still be easier to use than a copied file.')]),
22:('Sell Game Codes and Gift Cards on Shopify: Get the Workflow Right','Software & licences','A game activation code, a third-party prepaid code and a Shopify store gift card are different products. Define exactly what you are selling and confirm you are authorised to distribute it.',[
('Distinguish the code types','A Shopify gift card is store credit managed through Shopify’s gift-card features. A game or software code is redeemed with its publisher or platform. Delivering it through a licence-key app does not convert it into a native Shopify gift card.'),
('Verify the supply and restrictions','Use authorised inventory and keep documentation of its origin. State platform, region, edition, redemption deadline and eligibility restrictions where they apply. Do not imply a code is worldwide or permanent unless the issuer’s terms support that claim.'),
('Test one controlled redemption','Check that the code format, product mapping and customer instructions work together. Avoid consuming a live code casually during setup; use a test code or an agreed test process. Keep redeemed and available inventory distinct.'),
('Plan for support and refunds','Write a process for an invalid code, regional mismatch and alleged prior redemption. Keep the minimum evidence needed to investigate. Any revocation or refund policy must reflect the issuer’s terms and the applicable customer rules.')]),
23:('Sell Lightroom Presets on Shopify: Compatibility and Delivery','Design & templates','A preset pack should tell photographers what look it creates, which workflow it supports and how to install it. Good preview images and accurate compatibility information do more than a large preset count.',[
('Test the target Lightroom workflow','Identify the Lightroom product and versions you support. Preset import and file formats vary by workflow, so follow Adobe’s current instructions and test on the supported desktop or mobile setup. Do not label every export universally compatible.'),
('Show representative before-and-after images','Use photos you own or have permission to publish. Explain the starting conditions and any adjustments outside the preset. Avoid implying one preset will produce identical results across all cameras, lighting and exposure settings.'),
('Package a small installation guide','Include a readme, compatibility information and an example workflow. Organise files by supported use rather than leaving the buyer to guess. Tell customers where to look if an imported preset does not appear.'),
('Support the result, not a magic promise','Presets are starting points. Explain expected adjustments to exposure and white balance, and define the support you offer. A helpful sample preset can let a buyer test compatibility before purchasing the complete pack.')]),
24:('Launch a Music or Audio Pack on Shopify: A Delivery Checklist','Music & courses','A music release or sample pack needs more than an audio file. Buyers need to understand the contents, permitted uses, file specifications and how to retrieve the download reliably.',[
('Make the offer audible and precise','Publish a preview you have rights to share and list the number of tracks or samples. State file format, sample rate and bit depth where relevant. If stems, MIDI or project files are included, identify them separately.'),
('Write the licence before the sales copy','Listening rights, use in a video, commercial production and redistribution are different permissions. Explain the scope you are actually granting. Check rights for performances, compositions, samples and artwork before selling the pack.'),
('Prepare a scheduled release carefully','A timed album drop can use scheduled digital delivery. Confirm timezone, file mapping and the information preorder buyers receive. Run a controlled test before promising that every component unlocks together.'),
('Budget for the complete download','High-resolution audio and stems can make a pack large. Estimate bandwidth using the full purchase size and repeat downloads. Offer a readable contents file and a clear support route for interrupted downloads.')]),
25:('MP3, WAV or FLAC? Package Audio Downloads for Shopify','Music & courses','Choose audio formats for the buyer’s use, not just the smallest file. A listener, a producer and a customer buying stems may need different packages and download instructions.',[
('MP3 for convenient listening','MP3 uses lossy compression and generally makes smaller downloads. It can be useful for listening copies or previews. Describe the encoding quality and do not present it as identical to the original lossless master.'),
('WAV and FLAC for different lossless workflows','WAV commonly carries uncompressed PCM audio; FLAC uses lossless compression. Compatibility depends on the buyer’s software and devices. Test the exact files in the applications you say you support rather than relying only on the extension.'),
('A simple comparison','A listening edition might contain MP3s and artwork. A production edition might include WAV files, stems and a licence document. These are illustrative packaging choices, not a rule that every album needs multiple editions.'),
('Keep filenames and metadata coherent','Use consistent track numbers and names so a ZIP opens in a sensible order. Verify embedded metadata and artwork where supported. Keep the original masters backed up separately from the delivery files you publish.')]),
26:('Sell Notion Templates on Shopify: A Reliable Access Workflow','Design & templates','Selling a Notion template means helping the customer duplicate a usable workspace. The delivery link, sharing permissions and template contents all need to work for someone outside your own account.',[
('Clean the template before publishing','Remove private client data, secrets, personal notes and irrelevant pages. Replace example content with safe demonstration data. Check linked databases and external resources from a separate account so hidden dependencies do not break the product.'),
('Use a dedicated link for each sales channel','Notion’s guidance says a paid Marketplace template URL can redirect to its Marketplace checkout. For third-party sales, it recommends a separate copy and Notion Site link that customers can duplicate. Test your Shopify delivery link as a real buyer.'),
('Explain the first ten minutes','Include a short getting-started guide: duplicate the template, review example data and customise the key settings. State any Notion plan or external service requirements. A screen recording can help, but written steps should still stand alone.'),
('Set realistic access expectations','A delivered link can be shared. Notion’s Marketplace access-locking options are specific to its system; do not imply Shopify file delivery automatically provides those controls. Describe the licence and the support process clearly.')]),
27:('Sell Course Files on Shopify Without a Full Course Platform','Music & courses','You can sell a downloadable course as a collection of videos, audio and resources. Decide whether that format meets your teaching goals before assuming a file-delivery app can replace a learning platform.',[
('Know which learning features you need','Downloads can suit a workshop or self-paced resource pack. Progress tracking, quizzes, certificates, community access and student dashboards require separate verification. If these are essential, evaluate an LMS or a compatible course integration.'),
('Organise the lessons for self-guided use','Use a numbered contents file, clear lesson names and a suggested sequence. Keep videos in manageable sizes and include supporting PDFs. Explain how to resume learning after closing the download page.'),
('Make accessibility part of the package','Provide captions or transcripts where appropriate and readable exercise files. Test the download on mobile and a slower connection. A small preview lesson helps buyers assess format and teaching style before paying.'),
('Be precise about release timing','A scheduled release can unlock a product at a specified time. That is not automatically the same as a per-student drip schedule. Verify the exact behaviour before promising a lesson every week after each individual purchase.')]),
28:('Sell Printables on Shopify: From Export to a Good First Print','Design & templates','A printable is successful when it produces the expected result on the buyer’s printer. Clear dimensions and a tested file matter as much as the product mockup.',[
('Export for the intended paper size','Offer the paper sizes you actually support, such as A4 and US Letter, and label them clearly. Check margins, bleed if relevant, font embedding and whether the design remains readable in grayscale.'),
('Print the product yourself','Test at actual size rather than only viewing the PDF. Check cut lines, writing space and small text. Include simple instructions for scaling and duplex printing when needed, without assuming every printer uses the same controls.'),
('Show exactly what is included','List pages, formats, sizes and editability. A flat PDF is different from an editable Canva template. Make clear that no physical product ships, and explain the personal or commercial licence included.'),
('Deliver an organised pack','Use descriptive filenames and include a short readme. Consider a low-ink version when it helps the use case. If you stamp the PDF, test that the stamp does not cover functional areas such as writing lines or cutting guides.')]),
29:('Sell Seasonal Digital Products Without Starting Over Every Season','Ideas & growth','Seasonal products are easier to maintain when dates, artwork and delivery are treated separately. Build an update process around the buyer’s planning window, not only the event day.',[
('Create a reusable core','Keep the underlying worksheet, layout or workflow separate from dates and seasonal copy. A planner with editable dates can reduce the next update to a controlled revision instead of a full redesign.'),
('Plan the buyer’s timeline','A teacher, event organiser and last-minute party host shop at different times. Work backwards from when each needs the finished product. Use your own results to refine the launch window rather than assuming every seasonal item follows one calendar.'),
('Track what becomes stale','Maintain a checklist for years, weekdays, fixtures, links and promotional claims. After the event, remove urgency that is no longer true. Explain whether an old edition remains useful or has been replaced.'),
('Measure contribution, not just launch revenue','Include design time, paid acquisition, support and any usage costs in the review. A seasonal spike can look attractive while consuming disproportionate effort. Keep the products whose outcomes and economics justify another cycle.')]),
30:('Sports Canva Templates on Shopify: Updating a World Cup Collection','Design & templates','A sports template collection needs current information, original design and clear buyer instructions. With the 2026 World Cup complete, update the offer for an honest post-event or future-use purpose.',[
('Remove stale event promises','Review dates, fixtures and claims about upcoming matches. If the template is now a keepsake, say so. If it is reusable for another competition, remove event-specific data instead of changing only the title.'),
('Check two separate sets of rights','Canva’s content licence governs the assets used in the design. Competition marks, team logos, player images and other sports branding can involve separate rights. A Canva subscription does not automatically grant permission for all sports branding.'),
('Deliver the editable template safely','Use a template link that gives buyers their own copy, with a short PDF explaining how to edit it. Test with a separate account and disclose whether Canva Pro content or paid functionality is required.'),
('Design for reuse','Offer editable score fields, generic team placeholders and sizes appropriate for the stated use. A social post, printable bracket and event poster have different export requirements. Test each one you advertise.')]),
31:('Set Up Software Downloads on Shopify: A Release-Day Checklist','Software & licences','A software launch should make it easy to choose the correct installer, understand the licence and recover from an installation problem. Treat delivery as part of the release process.',[
('Separate builds and versions','Keep installers named by product, operating system, architecture and version where relevant. Map the correct files to each Shopify variant. Do not replace a stable release with an untested build simply because the download link is convenient.'),
('Publish trustworthy installation instructions','Explain supported environments and normal installation steps. Use your platform’s appropriate signing and distribution practices. Do not tell customers to disable security tools as a routine workaround for an unclear warning.'),
('Test purchase and activation together','A successful file download is only one checkpoint. Verify the installer launches and any licence key activates the expected edition. Keep delivery failures and application defects distinguishable in support records.'),
('Prepare a rollback and support path','Back up the previous release and document how affected buyers can retrieve a working version. State your update policy and gather reproducible error details. A release note should explain meaningful changes without exposing customer data.')]),
32:('Use Shopify Discount Codes for Digital Products Without Hiding the Margin','Ideas & growth','Discounts can support a specific campaign, but a lower price does not automatically create a better business. Decide what behaviour you want to encourage and measure the result against a baseline.',[
('Give the code a job','A launch offer, an existing-customer bundle upgrade and an abandoned-checkout campaign serve different purposes. Use clear eligibility, expiry and usage limits. Avoid permanent fake urgency or a discount from a price you never actually charge.'),
('Calculate the contribution per sale','Subtract the discount, payment fees, app charges and campaign costs. For example, a 20% discount on a $25 product produces $20 of sales revenue before fees and costs. That arithmetic is not a forecast of conversion or profit.'),
('Test eligibility and combinations','Use Shopify’s current discount settings and verify the intended products, customer eligibility and combination rules. Test a mixed cart if the store sells physical goods too. Check that the digital-delivery app receives the correct order items.'),
('Review the right measures','Compare revenue after discounts, contribution, refund rate and support load, not just code redemptions. Separate new buyers from people who would have paid full price. End or revise the campaign when the evidence does not support continuing it.')]),
33:('PDF Stamping on Shopify: What It Can and Cannot Do for Ebook Piracy','Ebooks & PDFs','PDF stamping can make a downloaded ebook less anonymous and discourage casual redistribution. It cannot make a PDF impossible to copy or guarantee that every leak is traceable.',[
('Understand the deterrent','A stamp can associate a delivered copy with buyer or order information. Someone may still remove it, screenshot the book or share it privately. Use accurate language such as discourages sharing rather than piracy-proof.'),
('Choose the information carefully','Use the minimum appropriate customer information for the purpose and explain the practice to buyers. Avoid placing unnecessary personal data throughout a file that the customer may legitimately display or print.'),
('Test readability on the real PDF','Check pages with dark illustrations, small text and unusual dimensions. A stamp that obscures content damages the purchase. BIG’s documentation specifies an unprotected PDF for stamping, so test the delivery format before launch.'),
('Combine protection with service','Keep reasonable download limits and a recovery path for genuine buyers. When a file appears elsewhere, review the evidence before accusing a customer. A watermark is one signal; it is not a complete investigation or access-control system.')]),
34:('Automatically Watermark PDF Purchases on Shopify','Ebooks & PDFs','An automatic stamping workflow should produce a readable customer copy after a purchase without manual editing. Test the original document, stamp settings and delivery route together.',[
('Prepare an unprotected PDF','Keep a clean master and confirm that its pages render correctly. BIG’s public documentation says PDF stamping requires a PDF that is not password protected. Upload the actual PDF rather than assuming a PDF inside an archive will be processed the same way.'),
('Configure and test the stamp','Use the options exposed in the app and a controlled purchase. Check the buyer details, position and legibility across multiple page layouts. Do not rely only on an admin preview if the delivered file can be tested.'),
('Know the difference from a manual watermark','Our free PDF watermark tool adds the same text to every page in your browser. It is useful for preparing samples or reminders. It does not connect to Shopify orders or personalise each buyer’s copy; the in-app workflow handles purchase-based stamping.'),
('Document exceptions','Tell support how to handle a protected source PDF, an unreadable stamp or a buyer who cannot download. Keep the original backed up. Review the result again after changing the master file or its page dimensions.')]),
35:('PDF, Video or Template: Choose a Digital Product Format by Use Case','Ideas & growth','There is no format that always sells best. Choose the medium that helps the buyer achieve the outcome, then account for production effort, compatibility and delivery cost.',[
('Use a PDF when reading and reference matter','Guides, checklists and printable worksheets suit a document. Keep navigation, readable text and print needs in mind. Fixed layouts are predictable, but long documents can be awkward on small screens if not designed carefully.'),
('Use video when demonstration matters','A physical technique or software workflow can be easier to understand on screen. Include captions or a transcript where appropriate. Larger files increase download time and bandwidth, so test the experience before promising frictionless access.'),
('Use a template when the buyer needs a starting system','A working spreadsheet, design or workspace can save setup time. It also creates compatibility and onboarding requirements. Document required software, paid features and the steps to make a personal copy.'),
('Combine formats only when each has a role','A short demonstration plus a template and reference PDF can be coherent. A large bundle with no starting point can overwhelm buyers. Validate the core outcome first, then add formats that remove a specific obstacle.')]),
36:('Shopify Digital Products vs BIG: A Buyer’s Checklist','Compare','Shopify’s free app and BIG overlap on digital file delivery. The decision is whether specialised workflows justify a paid plan for your particular store.',[
('Use a current baseline','The official Shopify app now describes file and link delivery, variants, download limits and customer-account access. Do not rely on a comparison that assumes the older product has never changed.'),
('Test the BIG-specific requirements','Try the actual workflow you need: an automatically stamped PDF, a unique licence key, a custom commission or a scheduled release. Include imports and exports if this is a migration rather than a new store.'),
('Model the paid tier honestly','BIG’s paid plans start at $9.99, but APIs and webhooks require Growth or Enterprise. Storage and monthly bandwidth remain limited by plan even when order counts are unlimited. The free Shopify app may be the better budget fit for basic delivery.'),
('Decide after a controlled purchase','Compare the email, mobile download and post-purchase access using the same product. Record any manual work required. Move only when the resulting benefit is clear enough to justify the new cost and migration effort.')]),
37:('Shopify’s Native Digital Products App: Capabilities and Gaps to Check','Compare','A fair review of Shopify’s own app starts with the current listing. Its capabilities have changed, so categorical claims copied from older articles can mislead a buyer.',[
('What the current listing documents','Shopify Digital Products describes digital files and links, delivery associated with products and variants, download limits and customer-account access. It is free. These are meaningful capabilities for a straightforward digital store.'),
('What needs more investigation','The listing does not document the same dedicated PDF-stamping, licence-inventory and custom/scheduled workflows that BIG describes. An undocumented capability is not proof that no configuration or integration can provide it; check your exact requirement.'),
('Avoid unsupported performance claims','A comparison should not invent complaint rates, outage histories or revenue losses. Test a representative file and inspect your own customer experience. If you have a failure, record what happened rather than assuming every merchant sees the same result.'),
('Choose the smallest workable setup','Start with the free app if it meets your needs. Consider BIG when specialised delivery or operational tools solve a real gap. Keep an evidence-based list of those gaps so the choice can be revisited as both products evolve.')]),
38:('Sports and Seasonal Printables: Build a Reusable Shopify Catalogue','Design & templates','A sports printable should be easy to update, easy to print and useful beyond one search spike. Plan the reusable design separately from competition dates and licensed branding.',[
('Start with original generic formats','A practice planner, match journal, score sheet or team-organiser checklist can solve a real task without relying on official logos. Define who uses it and where: at home, on the sidelines or during an event.'),
('Keep dates in a reviewable layer','Separate dates, fixtures and team names from the core layout. Verify event information against an official source before publication. After the season, remove outdated urgency and clearly label any archived edition.'),
('Test the physical output','Print the promised sizes, check writing space and offer a low-ink option when useful. A colourful screen preview may not work well on a household printer. Include instructions that match the intended use.'),
('Build repeat sales around improvement','Use buyer feedback to refine the next edition. Explain what changed rather than silently republishing the same file with a new year. If previous customers receive an update, state that policy clearly and test how delivery works.')]),
39:('Shopify Download Emails Going to Spam? Diagnose the Delivery Chain','Delivery','An email marked as sent is not the same as an email placed in the inbox. Diagnose the sender, the message and the customer’s alternative access route before changing the delivery app.',[
('Check the destination and sending event','Confirm the customer’s address, the order state and whether the delivery message was actually sent. A typo, delayed custom product or scheduled release is different from spam filtering. Resend only after understanding the likely cause.'),
('Authenticate the sender using provider instructions','If you use a custom sender, follow the sending provider’s current SPF, DKIM and DMARC setup instructions. Do not add guessed DNS records or duplicate SPF records. Authentication helps establish identity, but it does not guarantee inbox placement.'),
('Keep the message recognisable','Use a consistent sender, a clear purchase-related subject and a simple route to the download. Avoid unrelated promotional content in the delivery message. Test with more than one email provider and review the app’s available delivery information.'),
('Offer another way to retrieve the product','Verify post-purchase access and explain how a customer can recover their order. Keep a short support procedure for verifying the buyer and restoring access. A backup route reduces reliance on email without pretending that spam filtering can be eliminated.')])
}
